# sendiri hanya)KANTOR:** Ketika `TLS_MODE == self_signed`, perintah backend
# (dalam `templates/compose.yml.j2`) impor ke dalam CA ke dalam boleh tulis
# `cacerts` salinan dan titik JVM di atasnya via `JAVA_TOOL_OPTIONS`. Yang
# dibagikan `with-ca-trust.sh` Titik masuk mencakup OS/NSS/env toko
# kepercayaan dan bukan toko kepercayaan JVM, jadi tanpa ini PenpotPanggilan
# oIDC token/pengguna info server ke Keycloak ♪ Gagal dengan ♪ `PKIX path
# building failed`. Pembatalan dilakukan di gerbang belakang mode self-signed
# (Ini bukan operasi produksi, di mana cert yang asli ditandatangani CA sudah
# dipercaya) Jalur CA dikode keras karena kerangka kerja CA-override kembali
# menjalankan perintah.
msgid "**OIDC JVM CA trust (self-signed TLS only):** when `TLS_MODE == self_signed`, the backend command (in `templates/compose.yml.j2`) imports the internal CA into a writable `cacerts` copy and points the JVM at it via `JAVA_TOOL_OPTIONS`. The shared `with-ca-trust.sh` entrypoint covers the OS/NSS/env trust stores but not the JVM truststore, so without this Penpot's server-side OIDC token/userinfo calls to Keycloak fail with `PKIX path building failed`. The override is gated behind self-signed mode (it is a no-op in production, where real CA-signed certs are already trusted) and the CA path is hardcoded because the framework's CA-override re-serialises the command."
msgstr ""

# sendiri hanya)KANTOR:** Ketika ``TLS_MODE == self_signed``, perintah backend
# (dalam ``templates/compose.yml.j2``) impor ke dalam CA ke dalam boleh tulis
# ``cacerts`` salinan dan titik JVM di atasnya via ``JAVA_TOOL_OPTIONS``. Yang
# dibagikan ``with-ca-trust.sh`` Titik masuk mencakup OS/NSS/env toko
# kepercayaan dan bukan toko kepercayaan JVM, jadi tanpa ini PenpotPanggilan
# server-side OIDC token/pengguna info ke Keycloak ♪ Gagal dengan ♪ ``PKIX
# path building failed``. Pembatalan dilakukan di gerbang belakang mode
# self-signed (Ini bukan operasi produksi, di mana cert yang asli
# ditandatangani CA sudah dipercaya) Jalur KA ini dikodekan dengan keras
# karena jalur CA - override - re-serialisasi perintah itu.
msgid "**OIDC JVM CA trust (self-signed TLS only):** when ``TLS_MODE == self_signed``, the backend command (in ``templates/compose.yml.j2``) imports the internal CA into a writable ``cacerts`` copy and points the JVM at it via ``JAVA_TOOL_OPTIONS``. The shared ``with-ca-trust.sh`` entrypoint covers the OS/NSS/env trust stores but not the JVM truststore, so without this Penpot’s server-side OIDC token/userinfo calls to Keycloak fail with ``PKIX path building failed``. The override is gated behind self-signed mode (it is a no-op in production, where real CA-signed certs are already trusted) and the CA path is hardcoded because the framework’s CA-override re-serialises the command."
msgstr ""

