# per-role, saya ingin setiap peran yang `meta/services.yml` \"Menyatakan\"
# `ldap.enabled` (literal `true` Kedinamisan atau dinamis `"{{
# 'svc-db-openldap' in group_names }}"` bentuk) Ke kapal skenario Playwright
# yang menggunakan jalur login LDAP-bind end-to-end, sehingga varian LDAP dari
# stack autentikasi peran diverifikasi secara independen dari counterpart
# OIDC-nya.
# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "As a contributor maintaining the per-role Playwright suite, I want every role whose `meta/services.yml` declares `ldap.enabled` (literal `true` or the dynamic `\"{{ 'svc-db-openldap' in group_names }}\"` form) to ship a Playwright scenario that exercises the LDAP-bind login path end-to-end, so that the LDAP variant of the role's authentication stack is verified independently from its OIDC counterpart."
msgstr "Sebagai kontributor mempertahankan suite Playwright per-role, saya ingin setiap peran yang `meta/services.yml` \\\"Menyatakan\\\" `ldap.enabled` (literal `true` Kedinamisan atau dinamis `\"{{ 'svc-db-openldap' in group_names }}\"` bentuk) Ke kapal skenario Playwright yang menggunakan jalur login LDAP-bind end-to-end, sehingga varian LDAP dari stack autentikasi peran diverifikasi secara independen dari counterpart OIDC-nya."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "As a contributor maintaining the per-role Playwright suite, I want every role whose login flow is RBAC-gated (OIDC and/or LDAP) to also exercise the canonical non-admin user `biber` end-to-end, so that the RBAC plumbing from [004 - Generic RBAC role auto-provisioning](README.md#archive) is verified per role rather than only on the privileged-admin path."
msgstr "Sebagai kontributor mempertahankan suite per-role Playwright, saya ingin setiap peran yang aliran log masuk adalah RBAC-gated (OIDC dan/atau LDAP) untuk juga melatih pengguna non-admin kanonik `biber` Akhir-ke-akhir, sehingga pipa RBAC dari [004 - Provisi otomatis peran RBAC generik](README.md#archive) Keterbuktian setiap peran daripada hanya pada jalur hak istimewa-admin."

# setiap peran yang dimiliki kapal-kapal tingkat aplikasi untuk menyatakan
# mereka melalui satu terpadu `meta/addons/` Kontrak kontrak kontrak (1 file
# per addon), daripada ejaan per-app hari ini (`addons`, `plugins`,
# `extensions`, `modules`, `mu_plugins`) Diseberang `meta/services.yml`,
# `vars/main.yml`, Dan `tasks/`, sehingga addon dapat ditemukan, lintable, dan
# diuji dengan skema tunggal, dan sehingga setiap addon yang jembatan ke peran
# lain menyatakan bahwa ketergantungan secara eksplisit melalui bendera
# layanan dalam `meta/services.yml`.
msgid "As a contributor to Infinito.Nexus, I want every role that ships application-level extensions to declare them through one unified `meta/addons/` contract (one file per addon), instead of today's per-app spelling (`addons`, `plugins`, `extensions`, `modules`, `mu_plugins`) scattered across `meta/services.yml`, `vars/main.yml`, and `tasks/`, so that addons are discoverable, lintable, and testable with a single schema, and so that any addon that bridges into another role declares that dependency explicitly through a service flag in `meta/services.yml`."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "As a contributor, I want a requirements template so that new requirements are consistent and machine-readable."
msgstr "Sebagai kontributor, saya ingin sebuah templat persyaratan sehingga persyaratan baru adalah konsisten dan mudah dibaca mesin."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "As a developer, I want to run the Infinito.Nexus CI on a dedicated server so that the deploy + test cycle is no longer bound by local hardware restrictions."
