msgid "Both keys are optional. `modes: []` or no `modes` key means every network, and no `single_mode` key means `false`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Both layers are exhaustive over what the repository declares, which is exactly why the backlog lives outside them: an **open** pair, where a verified upstream plugin exists but nothing declares it, has no generated representation at all. Moving a pair from open to declared is the per-role upstream survey, and that survey is itself an acceptance criterion of this requirement (a MediaWiki deep-dive, for instance, added `DiscourseSsoConsumer`, `PeerTubeEmbed`, `MachineTranslation`→libretranslate, `Extension:AWS`→minio and an LLM editor→openwebui). [027-integration-matrix.md](027-integration-matrix.md) states where each layer's truth lives and why no frozen copy of the map is kept."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Both layers are process-wide in-process caches. They intentionally do NOT track on-disk file mtimes; CLI tools are short-lived and the assumption \"the on-disk file does not change while my process runs\" holds. The single exception is `utils.cache.yaml.dump_yaml`, which writes through and evicts the cached entry for the path it just wrote so a tool that edits a file mid-run sees the new content on the next read."
msgstr "Kedua lapisan tersebut adalah proses-luas dalam-proses cache. Mereka sengaja TIDAK melacak di-disk file waktu; CLI alat berumur pendek dan asumsi \"Berkas on-disk tidak berubah ketika proses saya berjalan\" Pegang. pengecualian tunggal adalah `utils.cache.yaml.dump_yaml`, yang menulis melalui dan mengusir entri cached untuk jalur itu hanya menulis sehingga alat yang mengedit file pertengahan-run melihat konten baru pada bacaan berikutnya."

msgid "Both markers are looked for on the construct's own line and across every contiguous comment line directly above it, in either order. This is the placement for an exemption that has to say *why*: the reason rarely fits beside the value, so it is written as a comment block above it, and :func:`is_suppressed_at` would only see the last line of that block."
msgstr ""

msgid "Both modes MUST keep a minimum age that outlasts every timeout of the application, so nothing an in-flight operation still writes is removed. `pressure` MAY only shorten ages, never drop them to \"now\". The one exception is a native command that drops a cache the application regenerates on demand, such as Nextcloud's `occ preview:cleanup`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Both name a Frappe doctype the image already ships, and the per-addon hooks [`tasks/addons/social_login_key.yml`](./tasks/addons/social_login_key.yml) and [`tasks/addons/email_account.yml`](./tasks/addons/email_account.yml) apply it through the bench python scripts [`oidc_settings.py`](./files/python/apply/oidc_settings.py) and [`email_account.py`](./files/python/apply/email_account.py)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Both name a Frappe doctype the image already ships, and the per-addon hooks ```tasks/addons/social_login_key.yml`` <./tasks/addons/social_login_key.yml>`__ and ```tasks/addons/email_account.yml`` <./tasks/addons/email_account.yml>`__ apply it through the bench python scripts ```oidc_settings.py`` <./files/python/apply/oidc_settings.py>`__ and ```email_account.py`` <./files/python/apply/email_account.py>`__."
msgstr ""

msgid "Both name surfaces EspoCRM ships itself, so their payload stays with [`templates/env.j2`](./templates/env.j2), which renders `ESPOCRM_CONFIG_OIDC_*` and `ESPOCRM_CONFIG_SMTP_*` from the same service flags the addons' `enabled` expressions read; [`files/php/seed/config.php`](./files/php/seed/config.php) writes them into EspoCRM's own config."
msgstr ""

msgid "Both name surfaces EspoCRM ships itself, so their payload stays with ```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__, which renders ``ESPOCRM_CONFIG_OIDC_*`` and ``ESPOCRM_CONFIG_SMTP_*`` from the same service flags the addons’ ``enabled`` expressions read; ```files/php/seed/config.php`` <./files/php/seed/config.php>`__ writes them into EspoCRM’s own config."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Both need the same facts about a role: whether it ships its own container stack, and which deploy modes it supports. Keeping the logic here means the two callers never drift."
msgstr "Kedua-duanya membutuhkan fakta yang sama tentang peran: apakah itu kapal-kapal kontainernya sendiri stack, dan yang menyebarkan mode yang didukungnya. Keeping logika di sini berarti dua penelepon tidak pernah hanyut."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Both on the position"
msgstr "Kedua-duanya pada posisi"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Both paths elevate privileges via `sudo` when not run as root, and the script verifies `bwrap` and `socat` on `PATH` before it exits. macOS uses `sandbox-exec` from the base system and does not need this target."
msgstr "Kedua-dua jalur mengangkat hak istimewa melalui `sudo` Ketika tidak dijalankan sebagai root, dan skrip diverifikasi `bwrap` Dan `socat` Pada `PATH` Sebelum keluar. Penggunaan macOS `sandbox-exec` Dari sistem dasar dan tidak membutuhkan target ini."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Both platforms run model-generated code, which is untrusted, so a kernel-level boundary is required on top of their in-app sandboxing. [gVisor](https://gvisor.dev/) provides that boundary behind an OCI runtime, so each agent app stays a normal container spec and only pins `runtime: runsc`, reusing the existing image pipeline, replicas, healthchecks, and dual-mode machinery. [Kata Containers](https://katacontainers.io/) wrapping Firecracker was the original choice; Decision #2 records why it is unreachable on this container engine. ([E2B](https://github.com/e2b-dev/infra) is the higher-level alternative but brings its own Nomad/Consul orchestration and x86-cloud self-host, which would replace the swarm model.)"
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Both pools feed the assignment, so narrowing `distros` to one value pins every row to it rather than reducing the run."
msgstr "Kedua kolam memberi makan tugas, begitu sempit `distros` Satu nilai pin setiap baris untuk itu daripada mengurangi lari."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Both renderers fail loudly when Jinja markers cannot be resolved so generated configs never silently leak unrendered placeholders."
msgstr "Kedua-dua renderer gagal keras ketika penanda Jinja tidak dapat diselesaikan sehingga konfigurasi yang dihasilkan tidak pernah diam-diam bocor pemegang tempat yang tidak dirender."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Both requirement files name the same collections at the same versions: the Galaxy file is the normal source, the git file the fallback used when galaxy.ansible.com is unreachable. A bump that touches only one of them would make the fallback install something the pin does not describe, so an update is applied to both or to neither."
msgstr "Kedua-duanya berkas persyaratan nama koleksi yang sama pada versi yang sama: berkas Galaxy adalah sumber normal, berkas git fallback digunakan ketika galaxy.ansible.com Tak bisa dicapai. Sebuah tonjolan yang menyentuh hanya salah satu dari mereka akan membuat fallback memasang sesuatu yang tidak dijelaskan pin, sehingga sebuah update diterapkan untuk keduanya atau untuk keduanya."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Both run from the trusted workflow ref and check out the version tag for the actual build payload, so the release artefacts match the tagged commit byte-for-byte."
msgstr "Kedua-duanya dijalankan dari ref workflow yang dipercaya dan memeriksa tag versi untuk muatan build aktual, sehingga artifak rilis cocok dengan yang ditag commit byte-for-byte."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Both sections are merged per entry, so an inventory that names one field keeps the rest of the declaration, and a key nobody declared is added."
msgstr "Kedua-dua bagian digabung per entri, jadi sebuah inventori yang menamai satu bidang menyimpan sisa deklarasi, dan kunci tidak ada yang dinyatakan ditambahkan."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Both sides pass `primary_apps` (not the round closure) as the BFS seed and the variant-merged services map for that round, so the reachability walk sees the same topology the inventory baked."
msgstr "Kedua belah sisi lulus `primary_apps` (Tidak ada penutupan bulat) Waafford sebagai benih BFS dan peta layanan yang dimunculkan varian untuk putaran tersebut, sehingga jalan yang dapat dijangkau melihat topologi yang sama yang dipanggang inventaris."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Both sources carry the same pinned collections, so the only thing separating them is how long they take and whether they answer at all. A single slow day says nothing: galaxy.ansible.com degrades and recovers, and a git clone can stall on one runner. The default is therefore retuned only when a rolling window of daily samples shows one source durably behind the other."
msgstr "Kedua sumber membawa koleksi yang sama, jadi satu-satunya hal yang memisahkan mereka adalah berapa lama mereka mengambil dan apakah mereka menjawab sama sekali. Sebuah hari yang lambat mengatakan apa-apa: galaxy.ansible.com Klon git dapat mengulur waktu pada satu pelari. Oleh karena itu, defaultnya baru kembali apabila jendela rolling sampel harian menunjukkan satu sumber yang cukup baik di belakang yang lain."

# translated-by: libretranslate
#, no-python-format
msgid "Both targets (Debian changelog and the RPM ``%changelog`` section) are fully regenerated on every run from the kept entries plus an archived-releases notice that points at the documentation site and lists the archived versions and dates as plain text. The notice is folded into the body of the oldest kept entry (not appended after the last entry), because free text after the final entry is not valid changelog data and makes the native parsers warn. Because the package files are regenerated, they cannot drift from the CHANGELOG.md SPOT."
msgstr "Kedua-duanya sasaran (Unazlog Debian dan RPM ``%changelog`` bagian) Khayal sepenuhnya diregenerasi pada setiap larian dari entri yang disimpan ditambah catatan rilis-arsip yang menunjuk di situs dokumentasi dan mencantumkan versi arsip dan tanggal sebagai teks biasa. Surat pemberitahuan ini dilipat ke dalam tubuh tertua terus masuk (Tidak ada lagi setelah entri terakhir), karena teks bebas setelah entri akhir tidak valid changelog data dan membuat parser asli memperingatkan. Karena berkas paket itu regenerasi, mereka tidak bisa hanyut dari CHANGELOG.md SPOT."

