msgid "Cluster dumps (``database = '*'``) go through ``baudolo-restore cluster`` with the superuser of the instance’s cluster row in ``databases.csv``, before the single-database dumps. A cluster dump without that row, or with a consumer of any database it recreates still running, aborts the run before anything is replayed. Database mode is local-only — the credentials live in the target host’s own ``databases.csv``."
msgstr ""

msgid "Cluster dumps (`database = '*'`) go through `baudolo-restore cluster` with the superuser of the instance's cluster row in `databases.csv`, before the single-database dumps. A cluster dump without that row, or with a consumer of any database it recreates still running, aborts the run before anything is replayed. Database mode is local-only — the credentials live in the target host's own `databases.csv`."
