# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Each role in that closure is then narrowed to the variants that actually reach a seed: variant `i` of a role is kept only when round `i`'s closure — walked on the same variant-merged services maps [the matrix planner](../../../../cli/administration/deploy/development/inventory/planner.py) builds its rounds from, and therefore variant-aware at every generation of the chain — contains one of the seeds. A role whose variants do not all qualify enters the whitelist as a `role#0,2` selection token, so an image bump in a provider no longer redeploys the variants that switch that provider off. This applies to every auto-derived whitelist — the weekly update PRs, Dependabot, and any other diff-driven run — because they all resolve through this one path."
msgstr "Setiap peran dalam penutupan itu kemudian dipersempit dengan varian yang benar-benar mencapai benih: varian `i` Peran yang disimpan hanya ketika bulat `i`Penutupan 's — berjalan di peta layanan yang muncul varian yang sama [Matriks perencana](../../../../cli/administration/deploy/development/inventory/planner.py) Karena itu, setiap generasi dari rantai itu, ada salah satu benihnya. Peran yang variannya tidak semua memenuhi syarat masuk daftar putih sebagai `role#0,2` Token seleksi sifection, sehingga sebuah gambar berbenturan pada sebuah penyedia tidak lagi mengurut ulang varian yang mematikan penyedia tersebut. Ini berlaku untuk setiap daftar putih yang otomatis diturunkan — PR update mingguan, Dependabot, dan setiap diff-driven berjalan — karena mereka semua menyelesaikan melalui satu jalan ini."

msgid "Each role runs the variant :func:`resolve_round` settles on: the clamped round index, the supplied index for a primary app, or the index a `# variant-pin:` in force forces (see :mod:`utils.roles.applications.variant_pins`). Every host of :data:`PRIMARY_ONLY_SERVICE_KEYS` stays on only where a primary app's variant declares it; every other role has it off. Roles without variants are absent from the result so the resolver falls through to its disk-read path."
