# [pr.sh](../../../../../scripts/github/update/open/pr.sh) dibaca `APP_SLUG`
# Dari lingkungan dan menyelesaikan pengguna robot App melalui `gh api
# /users/<slug>[bot]`. ID log masuk dan pengguna numerik yang diselesaikan
# ditulis ke `git config user.name` Dan `git config user.email` Di dalam
# `<id>+<slug>[bot]@users.noreply.github.com` Formulir bahwa GitHub menerima
# untuk melakukan deverifikasi. ♪ Ketika ♪ `APP_SLUG` Tidak ditentukan, naskah
# jatuh kembali ke `github-actions[bot]` Identitas identitas. Cabang itu
# dicapai hanya ketika skrip diseru diluar aliran kerja, misalnya tes asap
# lokal di mana pemanggil telah menetapkan `GH_TOKEN` Untuk sesuatu selain
# dari token App.
msgid "[pr.sh](../../../../../scripts/github/update/open/pr.sh) reads `APP_SLUG` from the environment and resolves the App's bot user via `gh api /users/<slug>[bot]`. The resolved login and numeric user ID are written into `git config user.name` and `git config user.email` in the `<id>+<slug>[bot]@users.noreply.github.com` form that GitHub accepts for verified commits. When `APP_SLUG` is unset, the script falls back to the `github-actions[bot]` identity. That branch is reached only when the script is invoked outside the workflow, for example a local smoke test where the caller has set `GH_TOKEN` to something other than an App token."
msgstr ""

