# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``priority`` IS the retrigger: it names what failed. ``offset`` is recomputed rather than carried, but from the carried value up: the source run got a stretch behind its own offset green before its budget ran out, so the regular line resumes behind that stretch (:func:`cli.administration.deploy.ci.selections.resume_offset`) instead of repeating it, and never falls back behind where that run started. Everything else is carried verbatim, including ``whitelist``, so a retrigger of a scoped run stays inside that scope instead of quietly widening to the whole repository."
msgstr "``priority`` Itu nama yang gagal. ``offset`` Dimasukkan kembali ketimbang dibawa, tetapi dari nilai yang dibawa ke atas: sumber menjalankan mendapat peregangan di belakang offset sendiri hijau sebelum anggarannya habis, sehingga garis tetap melanjutkan di belakang yang meregang (:func:`cli.administration.deploy.ci.selections.resume_offset`) Alih-alih mengulanginya, dan tidak pernah jatuh kembali ke belakang di mana lari yang dimulai. Segala sesuatu yang lain dibawa verbatim, termasuk ``whitelist``, Jadi, penggirim ulang dari sebuah skop tetap berada di dalam ruang lingkup itu daripada diam-diam melebar ke seluruh repositori."

msgid "``profile_tasks`` prints its timestamp line when the NEXT task starts, so the ``(H:MM:SS.mmm)`` printed after header N is the duration of header N-1's task. The duration is therefore booked to the previous header, not the current one; the line is doubled by two callbacks, so only the first after each header is read; the last task's duration appears only in the run's RECAP and is not captured here."
