msgid "`meta/csp.yml` declares `connect-src.wss` and `worker-src.blob` under `flags`, which renders them as the quoted keywords `'wss'` and `'blob'`. The browser console of every page reports `The source list for the Content Security Policy directive 'connect-src' contains an invalid source: ''wss''. It will be ignored.` and the same for `'blob'` in `worker-src`, and in a conference `Creating a worker from 'blob:https://meet.<domain>/…' violates the following Content Security Policy directive: \"worker-src 'self' 'blob'\"`, followed by an `e2ee:E2EEContext` worker error (measured on the compose stack with `sso` disabled). Cause: flags are for keyword sources such as `unsafe-inline`, scheme sources need their colon. Options: declare both as whitelist entries (`\"wss:\"` under `connect-src`, `\"blob:\"` under `worker-src`), as `roles/web-app-nextcloud/meta/csp.yml` does for `blob:`."
msgstr ""

msgid "`meta/csp.yml` grants `unsafe-eval` for `script-src`: Knockout compiles every `data-bind` attribute with `new Function`, and without the grant the Knockout forms of the admin stay empty (\"Unable to parse bindings\", measured on the code form at `tfa/google/auth`). The grant covers the storefront too, which runs the same Knockout components. Open for the role's owner: keep it, or serve the admin under a policy of its own."
