msgid "pacman on an arch stack reads up to three cache directories. `INFINITO_CACHE_HOST_PACMAN_PATH`, written by [host_pacman_path.py](../../../utils/env/handlers/infinito/cache/host_pacman_path.py), is the first `CacheDir` of the host's `pacman-conf`, and only on a host whose `/etc/os-release` `ID` is exactly `arch` running an arch stack. On Manjaro, EndeavourOS and every other host, and on every stack that does not run pacman, the variable is empty and pacman uses the shared layer alone. When it is set, [compose/pacman.override.yml](../../../compose/pacman.override.yml) and [compose/swarm/pacman.override.yml](../../../compose/swarm/pacman.override.yml) mount it read-only at the same path, layered only together with the shared folder. `pacman.sh` lists it as the first `CacheDir`, the node's own download directory `<shared>/pacman/node-XXXXXX/` as the second and `<shared>/pacman/` as the third. `pacman.sh` creates the node download directory with `mktemp` on its first run and reuses the one already listed in `pacman.conf` on every later run. pacman finds a package in any of the three directories and downloads a missing one, `.part` file included, into the node download directory, the first one it can write. The `PostTransaction` hook `pacman.sh` writes to `pacman.d/hooks/infinito-shared-cache.hook` beside `pacman.conf` then renames every finished package and signature from the node download directory into `<shared>/pacman/` and leaves `.part` files there for the next resume. `pacman.sh` fails when `pacman.conf` sets `HookDir`. The disc-space cleanup runs `pacman -Sc` per writable `CacheDir`, so it never touches the read-only layer."
msgstr ""

